      "id": "Q3",
      "text": "When a whole-plaint review identifies a civil-adjudicable tenancy subject alongside a separate special-Act trust-inquiry prayer, the mere combination of those prayers does not itself justify rejecting the entire plaint; lawful restriction to tenancy issues and applications to relinquish other prayers are distinct procedural matters.",
